{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And afterwards she bore a daughter.</b> After Leah bore six sons she bore one daughter. The expression ואחר means 'and last,' as in (Genesis 33:?) ״ואחר נגש יוסף.״ Perhaps the intention here is an allusion to the last ה (of the divine name), and therefore it says ואחר — 'afterwards' — she bore him six sons, which are six upper extremities, corresponding to which there are lower extremities that are sealed with His name; last she bore a daughter, for the Shekhinah is comprised of six extremities, and behold she is the attribute of judgment (דין), and this is ״ותקרא את שמה דינה״ — two letters, the middle letters of the pronoun, are interwoven with two letters of the name of mercy, for she is the daughter of 'who is gold' (מי זהב). Or let us say that the intention is not this at all, but rather that when she gave birth to Zevulun she did not wish to descend and receive from the forces below him, and paid them no heed, since she had already received all the forces above, which are the essence. And this is what the masters of truth, blessed memory, said: 'Leah prayed and turned back into a female' — and their intention in this is to say that Leah was worthy of being given Yosef, but she did not wish it and turned back into a female, for she paid no heed to anything below Zevulun, and therefore she came to stumbling and what happened, happened." "<b>And according to</b> the plain sense (peshat), that which is said — she prayed and turned back into a female, for the honor of Rachel she did so — is what they said in Berakhot, chapter HaRo'eh (Berakhot 60a): she prayed within forty days. She said, 'Let not Rachel my sister be like one of the maidservants'; immediately it was turned about and became a daughter, as it is said: ״ותקרא את שמה דינה.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:34.246842747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}